  "steps": [
    "Cook the egg noodles in a pan of boiling salted water for 4 minutes then drain and rinse in cold water to stop any further cooking.",
    "While the noodles are cooking, spray a wok or large frying pan with low-calorie cooking spray and fry the onion, ginger, garlic and fresh chilli over a medium heat for 2–3 minutes until soft.",
    "Add the red pepper, beansprouts, carrot and pak choi and cook for 2–3 minutes more.",
    "In a mixing bowl, add chilli powder, garam masala, turmeric, cumin, soy sauce, fish sauce and mix together.",
    "Add the peanut butter powder to the bowl along with the cornflour, coconut milk alternative and lime juice and mix well.",
    "Add the noodles to the vegetables and stir until combined.",
    "Pour over the sauce, making sure to stir thoroughly until the vegetables and noodles are coated, and cook for a further 2–3 minutes to thicken the sauce. (Once the vegetables and noodles are ready, at this point you could let them cool, then freeze to have another day.) Serve sprinkled with the chopped coriander and chilli flakes."
